   "registryDependencies": [
    "https://design.how/r/lime/skill.json",
    "https://design.how/r/lime/portal.json"
   ],
   "docs": "Lime is scoped: its styles apply only inside an element with the class lime.\n1. Import the theme once, in the root layout, as its own stylesheet (not an @import in globals.css): import '@/components/lime/styles.css'\n2. Put className=\"lime\" on the element that holds Lime UI, usually <body>. Lime's classes work on the elements inside it, in your own code too, not on that element itself.\n3. Wrap the app inside that element in <LimePortalProvider> from '@/lib/lime/portal', so dialogs and menus keep the theme.\nDark mode: put data-theme=\"dark\" on the lime element or any ancestor, such as <html>. The theme does not follow the system setting (prefers-color-scheme) on its own.\nComponents: npx shadcn@latest add https://design.how/r/lime/<name>.json; https://design.how/r/lime/registry.json lists them all.",
